## Final Batch Clusters

### T-R054 — AI candidate scorecards (Kaizen)

- New: `src/hr_advisory/agents/scorecard_agent.py` — Kaizen `BaseAgent`
  with signature-based prompt, system-prompt boundaries (no protected
  attributes, no inventing qualifications), rating clamping 1–5,
  decision constrained to `{proceed, reject, further_interview}`,
  graceful LLM-error fallback.
- Endpoint: `POST /recruitment/candidates/{id}/scorecard/generate`
  (owner/hr_manager, rate-limited 10/min, full tenant isolation).
- Persistence: best-effort write to `ScorecardEntry` with
  `is_ai_generated=True` + `generation_id`.
- Frontend: candidate detail page with "Generate AI Scorecard" gated
  by Settings toggle (`arbor.ai-scorecards`); template picker; full
  results render.
- Tests: 12 in `tests/unit/test_scorecard_agent.py` (all mocked LLM,
  no real API calls).

### T-R055 — Google Calendar interview sync (full delivery)

- OAuth: `src/hr_advisory/integrations/google_calendar/oauth.py` with
  HMAC-signed state (15-min TTL, prevents cross-company callback hijack),
  auto-refresh credentials, `disconnect` revokes tokens.
- Sync service: `src/hr_advisory/integrations/google_calendar/sync.py` —
  `create_event/update_event/delete_event/fetch_event/watch_events`,
  best-effort error handling.
- Persistence: new `GoogleCalendarConnection` DataFlow model; new
  `google_event_id` column on `InterviewSchedule`.
- Endpoints: 5 under `/integrations/google-calendar/` — `auth-url`,
  `callback`, `status`, `disconnect`, `webhook` (constant-time channel
  token compare via `secrets.compare_digest`).
- Recruitment hooks: `schedule_interview` calls `sync.create_event`,
  `update_interview` calls `update_event` (or `delete_event` on
  `status=cancelled`). Wrapped so Calendar outages don't block
  interviewing.
- Frontend: Settings card with Connect (opens auth URL in new tab,
  listens for postMessage) / Disconnect.
- Tests: 16 in `tests/unit/test_google_calendar_sync.py`.
- Setup docs in `cluster-8a-google-calendar-sync.md` (Cloud project,
  consent screen, redirect URIs, env vars).

### Onboarding T196-T200 — Auto-assign + admin frontend

- T196: verified `auto_assign_default_onboarding(...)` already wired in
  `register-employee` (auth.py:597). Walks role-filtered steps, creates
  `OnboardingStepProgress` rows, copies preboarding tasks.
- T197: employees page already has Directory / Onboarding / Invitations
  tabs.
- T198 (NEW): admin template list page at `/onboarding` with create /
  edit / duplicate / set-default / archive.
- T199 (NEW): template builder at `/onboarding/templates/[id]` with
  module + step CRUD (numeric `sort_order` for reorder; drag-and-drop
  deferred per brief).
- T200 (NEW): assign-template button on Employees Onboarding tab with
  picker modal.

### Onboarding T201-T207 — Employee self-service UI

- T201: refactored `/my-onboarding` page with module-grouped step list
  + new `ProgressBar` (T204) with module-level tooltip.
- T202: 6 step renderers under
  `apps/web/src/components/onboarding/steps/` —
  `Content`, `Checklist`, `DocumentUpload`, `PolicyAcknowledgment`,
  `Form` (dynamic JSON-schema), `Approval`.
- T203: each renderer calls the correct backend endpoint and triggers
  a parent-level refresh.
- T205: `PreboardingChecklist` for HR/owner viewing
  `/my-onboarding?employee_id=N`.
- T206: side-nav entry verified.
- T207: `POST /onboarding/reminders/send-overdue` — Resend-backed
  digest emails, capped at 5 calls/hour/company,
  graceful skip when `RESEND_API_KEY` missing.

### Onboarding T208-T211 — Integrations + tests

- T208: shadow briefing now surfaces "X new hires onboarding (Y%
  complete on average)" + overdue alert for HR/owner; "Continue your
  onboarding" card for employees.
- T209: leave application returns soft `warning` field when employee
  is `on_probation` AND has an active onboarding assignment. Soft, not
  blocking.
- T210: `tests/integration/test_onboarding_flow.py` — full happy path
  against real Postgres (9 tests).
- T211: shadow agent `onboarding` intent + tool registry with
  `my_progress`, `list_assignments`, `list_templates`. Rule-based
  fallback handles "show my onboarding progress" etc.

### Onboarding phase B-D (T212-T220)

8 of 9 already done at HEAD; **T215 surfaced a real product bug**:

- 19 `datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()` calls in
  `routers/onboarding.py` were writing tz-aware ISO strings into the
  Postgres `timestamp without time zone` columns, which crashed every
  HTTP-path import / assign. Fixed inline.
- *(Note: the agent first replaced these with deprecated
  `datetime.utcnow()`, which broke the cluster-1 ban-utcnow regression
  test. Replaced again with `datetime.now(timezone.utc).replace(tzinfo=None)`
  — preserves UTC semantics + naive output + no deprecation warning.)*
- T215: `tests/integration/test_onboarding_e2e.py` — 7-test e2e flow
  Excel→template→assign→complete→completed against real Postgres.
- T214: `tests/regression/test_t214_preboarding_auto_create.py` locks
  in auto-assign + deadline math.
- T216-T220: pre-boarding UI, filters/export, buddy assignment, pulse
  surveys + frontend — all already at HEAD per the audit.

